# Local environment for Asset Hunter.
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is committed so the
# variable *names* are discoverable without their values. See docs/DEPLOY.md for
# what production needs.
#
# EmDash reads secrets from `process.env` at runtime, never from
# `import.meta.env` — the bare `import.meta.env` form is replaced at build time
# by a Vite literal, which would bake the value into the shipped bundle and
# shadow whatever the platform actually has configured.

# --- Required in production -------------------------------------------------

# Encrypts plugin secret settings at rest. Operator-provided, never stored in the
# database; losing it loses everything encrypted with it. Generate with:
#   npx emdash secrets generate
# Rotation is a comma-separated list, newest first: "new_key,old_key".
EMDASH_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# --- Optional ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Unset, EmDash generates each once and stores it in the options table. Set
# explicitly only if the value must survive a database replacement.

# HMAC secret for signing preview URLs.
EMDASH_PREVIEW_SECRET=
# Site-specific salt for hashing commenter IPs.
EMDASH_IP_SALT=

# --- Hunt engine (never deployed) -------------------------------------------
# Only needed for a real hunt. Unauthenticated GitHub search is limited to 10
# requests a minute, which is not enough.
#   export GITHUB_TOKEN=$(gh auth token)
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# --- Cloudflare (deploy tooling only, not read by the app) -------------------
# Read by `wrangler`. The Worker receives its own secrets via
# `wrangler secret put`, not from here.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
